// What a floor of the Undermere hides, and how hard each thing is to see:
// its secret doors and hidden rooms, walled over by `rl_mapgen::HideOpenings`
// in `dungeon.rs`'s chain. `src/traps.rs` loads this file. Floors one to
// nine hide things; the throne's floor hides nothing, so its fight is the
// one in plain sight. Every chance is a percent a turn while the thing is
// in sight, before `plugin.rs`'s spotting rules: whole within two cells,
// half out to seven, tripled on a turn spent waiting, and a ring of
// awareness's fifteen a level added to every roll.
//
// Every field:
//   secret_doors: (from:, count:, spot:), a loop's opening walled over, so a
//                 shortcut and never the way on
//     from:   the first floor that has any
//     count:  (fewest, most), drawn evenly for each floor from `from` on;
//             fewer where the floor has fewer loops safe to hide
//     spot:   the chance a turn, 0 to 100
//   hidden_rooms: (count:, spot:), a dead-end room's one door walled over, a
//                 pocket; a floor whose pool picks ask for a hidden room
//                 (`assets/pool.ron`'s `prefer: Hidden`) has at least one
//                 for each such pick, raised past `count`'s fewest
//     count:  (fewest, most), drawn evenly for each floor
//     spot:   the chance a turn, 0 to 100
(
    secret_doors: (from: 2, count: (1, 3), spot: 6),
    hidden_rooms: (count: (0, 2), spot: 5),
)
